/-
Weak: **PHASE 5, stage 2: CERTIFICATE (b) for `AxSpinE8.wpdMycpu` — the DIVERTED-RETURN STUCK
TWIN**, on a closed, computed S-mode instance, restated under O2 Stage C.

Rocq: `iris/AxSpinE8d.v` @ xxvzwolszwmp.

## The Rocq header, in substance

On a CLOSED instance (S-mode, Sv39, WARM TLB; the page table / state of `AxSpinSpikeRun`) a
COLD run of xv6's real `mycpu` warms the TLB; `rsE` = its final register file with PC := mycpu,
ra = `retOn` (0x80000000).  `rowM` = the label row of a warm run from `rsE` (generated by the
untrusted `AxScRun3.jtr` tracer), which IS a mycpu row (`rowMycpu`).  A row-generic DRIVER
(`rdrive`, §2, sound for the step relation `rowStuckR` quantifies over) runs the real
`riscvStep` on `rowM` from the boundary `rsE` at position 0 to the boundary just after mycpu's
c.ret: `reachOn` (reload values as in the row: PC = `retOn`, `pcOn`) and `reachOff` (the SAME
row, but ra's reload delivers the bytes of `retOff` = 0x80000010: the row-free opsem does not pin
read values, only the graph does; PC = `retOff`, `pcOff`).  THE TWIN: `divStuck` (the diverted
boundary is row-stuck, via `offrowRowStuck` with the arbitrary-VA premise replaced by computed
`frb` verdicts `frbOffT`/`frbOffF`, transferred to every register file agreeing off the pins by
`frbAgree`: `divFirstRead`), `divWpd` (hence `wpdM … .MaybeStuck` of that boundary for EVERY
postcondition, whenever the graph pins hart `i`'s row to `rowM`), `onNotStuck` (the MATCHING
return is not stuck: an administrative run to a read node that fits the row, `nsd`).
HONEST SCOPE (Rocq): the row generator and the warm-up are untrusted (only their outputs,
re-checked by the driver and the boolean checkers, are used); the certificate is about
`rowStuckR`, not a whole Ixv6 instance.

## Stage C / Q20' status — the twin is RESTATED, not dropped

With Rocq's LITERAL instance (two `c.nop` at the return site) the twin is FALSE under Stage C
(Q20', `notes/weak-port-q20-offrow.md` §C.2 item 3): Rocq's row is mycpu's 18 items + item 18 =
the FETCH of the return site, and that fetch item pinned the return.  Under Stage C fetches are
administrative (no row item), so the literal row is mycpu's 4 memory events and the post-c.ret
boundary sits AT the row end (position 4 = length): `div_stuck` fails (`rowStuckR` needs
`k < row.length`), `div_wpd` is unprovable (`wpdM` at the row end owes `postLifting Φ`, false at
`Φ := False`), `row_mycpu` fails (`RowMycpu` needs `k + 4 < row.length`), `nsd_on` fails (the
c.nops are followed by an image-less fetch at 0x80000004 and no read, by inspection of the
image), and `on_not_stuck` holds only vacuously (by the row-end conjunct).
A TRUE restatement exists and is what this file proves (deviation 1): the return site holds a
load (`ld a1,-8(sp)`) instead of the two `c.nop`, so the return site's first MEMORY event is the
row's item 4 — the Stage C counterpart of Rocq's item 18.  The diverted target 0x80000010 is
X-mapped by the spike's synthetic page table (page 0x80000 RWX) but has NO image bytes, so its
fetch is the no-image fetch `FirstRd.frNf` — exactly the owner's Q20 meaning ("a diverted fetch
outside the image is stuck"); the matching return reaches a read fitting item 4.  This is the
case the Q20 note (§B) calls reachable only for an abstract page table with an executable
mapping onto a non-text PA; it is not a statement about xv6's real table (Option V stands for
`wpdMycpu`).  This file is therefore a consumer of `AxSpinE9.frb` / `AxSpinE3.offrowRowStuck`.

## Deviations from Rocq

1. THE INSTANCE (above): `mem1` puts `ld a1,-8(sp)` (0xff813583) at `retOn` (Rocq: two
   `c.nop`); `rowM` has 5 items (Rocq 19): spills 0/1, reloads 2/3, the return site's load 4.
   Positions: Rocq `row_m_18` ↦ `rowM4` (item 4, a load of ra's slot), ra's reload item 13 ↦ 2
   (`ovOff`), the post-c.ret boundary 18 ↦ 4, `row_m_len` 19 ↦ 5.  `rowM` is a frozen literal as
   Rocq's `Eval vm_compute`; the Lean-only `AxSpinE8d.rowMGen` checks the generator produces it.
2. O2 STAGE C (fetches are administrative, pinned to the boot image): the driver takes the image
   (`rdrive img …`, `nsd img …`) and fetches go through `nodeStep2`'s image-answered admin arm;
   soundness (`rdriveSound`, `adminAstep`, `nsdReach`, `nsdNotStuck`) is for
   `AxSpinRow.astepPin (WeakAxRealize.fetchPin img) row` (Rocq `astep_any row T img` for every
   `T img`), via the Lean-only `AxSpinE8d.nodeStep2Pin`.  The instance statements are at the
   Lean-only image `AxSpinE8d.img1` (= `mem1`, `Int`-indexed); `divWpd` takes
   `HGimg : ∀ GD, G GD → GD.gdG.gxImg = img1` (as `AxSpinE3.wpdOffrowM`).  `rdNode` refuses
   fetches (`akIfetch`; Rocq `ak_coh`); `lbAdminB` also accepts `LIFetch`.
3. THE STOP: under Stage C c.addi/c.ret keep the row position, so the FIRST boundary at 4 is
   after `ld s0`; `rdrive` takes a boundary predicate `stop` and stops at the first boundary at
   `kend` with `stop rs` (Lean-only `AxSpinE8d.stopRet`: the PC has left mycpu).
4. `rdNode` matches the row item as `.LLoad` (Rocq: `aident lb = IRead …`, equivalent).
5. `run_on_eq`/`run_off_eq`: from the Lean-only `AxSpinE8d.runOnSome`/`runOffSome`
   (`isSome` by `decide +kernel`); Rocq's `Strategy opaque` line is not needed.
6. TYPES: `Interface.Ret tt` ↦ `.pure ()`; `st` ↦ `AxEpiRun.st`; `MState rs ∅ dev0_state` ↦
   `⟨rs, fun _ => none, testDevs⟩`; `regs_agree seip_reg` ↦ `regsAgree AxRunClose.pinReg`;
   `init_regstate` ↦ `AxSpinSpikeRun.spikeRegs0`; addresses `Nat` (as `AxSpinSpikeRun`);
   `S k` ↦ `k + 1`; `WPd s @ MaybeStuck; i {{ Φ }}` ↦ `wpdM rvwmoCatConsistent .MaybeStuck i s Φ`
   at any `hlc`; byte lists via the Lean-only `AxSpinE8d.b8`.  `vm_cast_no_check` ↦
   `decide +kernel`; the `Print Assumptions` lines are not ported (the lint covers them).

**Rocq → Lean name map** (all file-qualified `AxSpinE8d.*`: short generic names).  `jsteps`
`jsteps`, `ret_on` `retOn`, `ret_off` `retOff`, `mem1` `mem1`, `cold` `cold`, `entry` `entry`,
`rsE` `rsE`, `row_m` `rowM`, `row_m_len` `rowMLen`, `row_m_18` `rowM4`, `row_mycpu` `rowMycpu`,
`is_ret` `isRet`, `rd_node` `rdNode`, `rd_node_aread` `rdNodeAread`, `lb_admin_b` `lbAdminB`,
`lb_admin_b_sound` `lbAdminBSound`, `wr_fit` `wrFit`, `row_vals` `rowVals`, `rdrive` `rdrive`,
`admin_astep` `adminAstep`, `rdrive_sound` `rdriveSound`, `nsd` `nsd`, `nsd_reach` `nsdReach`,
`nsd_not_stuck` `nsdNotStuck`, `fuel0` `fuel0`, `off_bytes` `offBytes`, `ov_off` `ovOff`,
`run_on` `runOn`, `run_off` `runOff`, `rs_on` `rsOn`, `ib_on` `ibOn`, `rs_off` `rsOff`, `ib_off`
`ibOff`, `run_on_eq` `runOnEq`, `run_off_eq` `runOffEq`, `reach_on` `reachOn`, `reach_off`
`reachOff`, `pc_on` `pcOn`, `pc_off` `pcOff`, `p_off` `pOff`, `frb_off_t` `frbOffT`,
`frb_off_f` `frbOffF`, `Coff` `Coff`, `Coff_seip` `coffSeip`, `div_first_read` `divFirstRead`,
